Z||000000||87DUKE-L4||06-09-2001||01:33 PM||||I HAVE AN 87 L4 DIS IGNITION, MY PROBLEM IS THE CAR WON'T START UNLESS YOU SPRAY STARTING FLUID IN THE THROTTLE BODY. ONCE STARTED, THE ENGINE BOGS IF YOU THROTTLE IT TO FAST. ALTHOUGH, ONCE THE ENGINE WARMS UP, IT RUNS GREAT, IT WILL EVEN RESTART, UNTIL IT COOLS DOWN AGAIN. THEN IT'S BACK TO THE STARTING FLUID. THE ECM DUMPS NO CODES EXCEPT #12. PARTS I HAVE CHANGED OUT; <P>O2 SENSOR, INJECTOR, THROTTLE POSITION SENSOR, COOLANT TEMPERATURE SENSOR, MANIFOLD AIR PRESSURE, MANIFOLD TEMP SENSOR (FOUND ON THE RT. SIDE OF INTAKE), NEW FUEL PUMP, STRAINER AND FUEL FILTER, NEW BATTERY, NEW ALTERNATOR. NEW WIRES AND SPARK PLUGS, MOST PARTS ARE AC DELCO$$.<P>I'VE CHECKED THE INTAKE FOR ANY CRACKS OR LEAKS, NONE FOUND, CHECKED AND OR REPLACED THE VACUUM LINES. CHECKED AND CLEANED THE IDLE AIR CONTROL.     <P>Sorry about the caps<BR>ANY IDEAS? PLEASE HELP, LOST WITH A CAUSE.<p>[This message has been edited by 87DUKE-L4 (edited 06-09-2001).]||||reg||11
Z||000001||theogre||06-09-2001||09:14 PM||||Put a test light in terminal G of the ALDL. ground the other lead. It sounds like you have a fual pump power problem. Terminal G is the FP test point.<P>Crank the engine and see if the light comes on or how long it takes to come on.<P>Power problems to the FP are usually either the relay or the oil pressure sender. If the relay is shot then the pump will not turn on untill the oil pressure rises.||||reg||1
